These Python scripts help to detect whether files in the repository
conform to SPARTA coding conventions or not, and can fix those issues, too.
They are adapted from the LAMMPS tools/coding_standard scripts.

permissions.py   detects if sources and data files have executable permissions
whitespace.py    detects TAB characters and trailing whitespace
homepage.py      detects outdated SPARTA homepage URLs (pointing to the old Sandia site
                 instead of sparta.github.io) and developer emails
unicode.py       detects non-ASCII characters; -f replaces typographic characters
                 (curly quotes, dashes, ...) with ASCII, invisible and bidirectional
                 control characters must be removed by hand

Example usage: python3 whitespace.py <DIRECTORY> [-f]

where <DIRECTORY> is the path of a SPARTA directory containing subdirs src/, python/, doc/, etc.
They can also be run from the src/ folder with "make check" or "make check-<name>",
and "make fix-<name>" to apply the automatic fixes.
